{start_of_verse label="Verse 1"}
The [G]minstrel [C]boy to the [G]war is [D]gone,
In the [G]ranks of [Em]death you'll [Am]find [D]him;
His [G]father's [C]sword he has [G]girded [D]on,
And his [G]wild harp [C]slung be[D]hind [G]him;
'[Em]Land of [Bm]song!' said the [C]warrior [G]bard,
'Though [Em]all the [Am]world be[D]trays thee,
One [G]sword, at [C]least, thy [G]right shall [D]guard,
One [G]faithful [C]harp shall [D]praise [G]thee!'
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 2"}
The [G]Minstrel [C]fell! But the [G]foeman's [D]chain
Could [G]not bring his [Em]proud soul [Am]un[D]der;
The [G]harp he [C]loved ne'er [G]spoke a[D]gain,
For he [G]tore its [C]chords a[D]sun[G]der;
And said, '[Em]No [Bm]chains shall [C]sully [G]thee,
Thou [Em]soul of [Am]love and [D]bravery!
Thy [G]songs were [C]made for the [G]pure and [D]free,
They shall [G]never [C]sound in [D]slav[G]ery!'
{end_of_verse}
{x_end: G}
